<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar inflows $52.9 mln June 2.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar inflows $52.9 mln June 2.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $52.9 million surplus on June 2 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank data suplied to banks.</p>
<p>A banker with access to the figures said the Central Bank issued the following breakdown.</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON JUNE 2</p>
<p>Exports: $311.7 million</p>
<p>Imports: $306.4 million</p>
<p>Finanancial buy: $323.9 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $276.3 million</p>
<p>Net surplus: $52.9 million</p>
<p>Note: Figures rounded off.</p>
<p>((--Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroon, 55 11 2485418))</p>
</text>
